(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["me-easy-2026-006"]={"v":1,"id":"me-easy-2026-006","title":"Basic Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","sourceTitle":"Basic Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","branch":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING","code":"ME","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering","seriesId":"me-easy-2026","num":6,"category":"basic","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering"},"source":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Mechanical_Engineering/012_Basic Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>There are four types of candidates in an institute preparing for the UPSC. The number of students of Engineering, Science, Commerce and Humanities is 40, 60, 50 and 30 respectively and the respective percentage of students who qualified the UPSC is 80%, 75%, 60% and 50% respectively. The overall percentage of successful candidates in the institute is :</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"67.77%"},{"key":"B","html":"66.66%"},{"key":"C","html":"68.5%"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c572b8fd90262ce8f19.png\" /></div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MSQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The number 12375 is divisible by</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3"},{"key":"B","html":"9"},{"key":"C","html":"11"},{"key":"D","html":"7"}],"answer":["A","B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)<br />\n&bull; For a number to be divisible by 3 and 9, the sum of its digits should be divisible by 3 and 9<br />\nrespectively. Here, 1 + 2 + 3 + 7 + 5 = 18, which is divisible 3 and 9 both. Hence, the number is<br />\ndivisible by both 3 and 9.<br />\n&bull; For a number to be divisible by 11, the difference between the sum of digits in the odd<br />\npositions and even positions must be a multiple of 11 or 0. Here, (5 + 3 + 1) &ndash; (7 + 2) = 0. Hence,<br />\nthe number is divisible by 11.</p>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Number of even divisor of 5400.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"36"},{"key":"B","html":"48"},{"key":"C","html":"24"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8f/8f9036f2a4ceb7354851.png\" /></div>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In the given figure, ∠BAC and ∠BDC are the angles of same segments, ∠DBC = 30° and ∠BCD = 110°. ∠BAC is equal to </p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/02ea2b22bdc24ebceafe.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"35°"},{"key":"B","html":"40°"},{"key":"C","html":"55°"},{"key":"D","html":"60°"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/99691760b9c1b028cee8.png\" /></div>\n</div>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Sum of all numbers n such that n! ends with 30 zeros.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"610"},{"key":"B","html":"590"},{"key":"C","html":"614"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\n124! ends with 28 zeros and 125! ends with 31 zeros.<br />\nTherefore, there is no integer n with n! ending in exactly 30 zeros.</p>"},{"n":6,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/4689da9997b68e26e68b.png\" /></p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2 (2 - 2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/45/45d977661fe05c55d7f1.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the diagram given below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e8/e883276e1f9f9bc336c0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Five hundred candidates appeared in an examination comprising of tests in English, Hindi and Mathematics. The diagram gives the number of candidates who failed in different tests. The percentage of candidates who failed in at least two subjects is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.078"},{"key":"B","html":"1.0"},{"key":"C","html":"6.8"},{"key":"D","html":"7.8"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/82/826992f2a1fec813a92a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For the mirror represented by a line <em>MN</em>, choose the correct mirror-image of the figure, from amongst the four alternatives (a), (b), (c) and (d) given along with it.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f6828b0238a54662e652.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a9/a9b437bc1a19241d37e8.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/94/9454f4883848a05d37ce.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e3371ce9b448e4723409.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2d/2dc1f7c540fb97d32bf4.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Read the passage carefully and choose the best answer to the following question from the four alternatives given below.<br />\nAmong the natural resources which can be called upon in national plan for development, possibly<br />\nthe most important is human labour; without productive labour force, including effective leadership<br />\nand intelligent middle management, no amount of foreign assistance or natural wealth can ensure<br />\nsuccessful development and modernisation. One essential factor is usually overlooked or ignored.<br />\nThe forgotten factor is the role of women. Development will be handicapped as long as women<br />\nremain second-class citizens, uneducated, without any voice in family or community decisions,<br />\nwithout legal or economic status, married when they are still practically children, and thenceforth<br />\nproducing one baby after another, often only to see half of them die before they are of school age.<br />\nWe can enhance development by improving ‘woman power’ by giving women opportunity to develop themselves.<br />\nThe most important natural resource for national development is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"human labour"},{"key":"B","html":"effective leadership"},{"key":"C","html":"intelligent middle management"},{"key":"D","html":"foreign assistance"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nThe passage clearly states that among natural resources, human labour is the most important for national development.</p>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In the following question, a part of the sentence is given in bold. Choose the correct alternative that best improves the bold part. If no improvement is needed, select “No improvement.”<br />\nHe likes to drive his car at a speed of eighty kilometres <strong>each hour.</strong></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"in every hour"},{"key":"B","html":"an hour"},{"key":"C","html":"hourly"},{"key":"D","html":"No improvement"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nThe correct expression is &ldquo;eighty kilometres an hour&rdquo; (or per hour). The word &ldquo;each&rdquo; is<br />\ngrammatically incorrect in this context. &ldquo;Correct sentence: &ldquo;He likes to drive his car at a speed of<br />\neighty kilometres an hour.&rdquo;</p>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A gas turbine cycle operates on Brayton cycle with pressure ratio of 9.3. If the specific heat capacities at constant pressure for heat addition and heat rejection processes are 1.31 kJ/kgK and 0.98 kJ/kgK, then the thermal efficiency of the cylce is<br />\n[Take average value of γ = 1.41 for working fluid undergoing any process within the cycle]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"60.885%"},{"key":"B","html":"47.714%"},{"key":"C","html":"37.33%"},{"key":"D","html":"48.938%"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/708229b05d04888daf52.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A cantilever beam of 4 m span carries a uniformly distributed load over the entire length. If the deflection at the free end is 30 mm, then the slope at the free end is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.005 rad"},{"key":"B","html":"0.008 rad"},{"key":"C","html":"0.0085 rad"},{"key":"D","html":"0.01 rad"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/65/65979d58a9b2daa3fb03.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The disk starts from an initial angular velocity of 1 rad/s at θ = 0° and is subjected to an angular acceleration of α = (0.3θ) rad/s<sup>2</sup>, where θ is in radians. The magnitudes of the normal and tangential components of acceleration of a point P on the rim of the disk when the disk has rotated through one revolution are</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ad/adc3578c304a27efc69b.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b2/b28352cd408e910297c3.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d9/d9cf29468b40b3e1dbb3.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/775ad4c0090d4f073ac9.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f9/f9519ba6018ba77c6a14.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6e/6eb69f3e7b15112ca6ac.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f3bc2629d88533309870.png\" /></div>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The relative amounts of ferrite and cementite in pearlite in microstructure of eutectoid steel are</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"77% and 23% respectively"},{"key":"B","html":"67% and 33% respectively"},{"key":"C","html":"82% and 18% respectively"},{"key":"D","html":"88% and 12% respectively"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd81fc85c82ca20a414c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":15,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In jigs and fixtures, typical locating devices for circular or semicircular jobs used are</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"angle plates"},{"key":"B","html":"V-blocks"},{"key":"C","html":"mandrels"},{"key":"D","html":"metal pins"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nIn jigs and fixtures, workpieces having circular or semicircular profile are located by means of a<br />\nV-block. The V-block should be used correctly so that the variations in the work piece size are not<br />\ndetrimental to location. V-blocks can be used both for locating and clamping a work piece.</p>"},{"n":16,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A stream of moist air at 2°C DBT and 80% RH mixes with another stream of moist air at 30°C DBT and 10°C DPT in the ratio by mass of one part of the first to two parts of the second. The enthalpy of the air after mixing is<br />\n[Take : ω<sub>a</sub> = 0.0035 kgw.v./kgd.a. and <em>h</em> = 10.78 kJ/kgd.a. at 2°C DBT and 80% RH, ω = 0.00765 kgw.v./kgd.a. and <em>h</em> = 49.67 kJ/kgd.a. at 30°C DBT and 10°C DPT]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"30.35 kJ/kgda"},{"key":"B","html":"36.86 kJ/kgda"},{"key":"C","html":"33.31 kJ/kgda"},{"key":"D","html":"31.31 kJ/kgda"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/95/9544fa7d8f5f326e0e5d.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/7891ff7101609957e4ab.png\" /></div>"},{"n":17,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The equivalent stiffness of spring-mass system as shown in figure is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/70400f16cad68ff7020f.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"4 k"},{"key":"B","html":"13 k"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0f/0fda91b602f2f7d62fd0.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"11 k"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/01/01142301c501410d5d88.png\" /></div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For a refrigerant, at 20°C the specific volume of saturated vapour and saturated liquid are 0.036 m<sup>3</sup>/kg and 0.0008 m<sup>3</sup>/kg respectively. If the saturation pressures at 25°C and 15°C are 650 kPa and 510 kPa, then the enthalpy of vapourization of refrigerant is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"9.856 kJ/kg"},{"key":"B","html":"147.672 kJ/kg"},{"key":"C","html":"144.39 kJ/kg"},{"key":"D","html":"295.5 kJ/kg"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6d/6d62e2654e329565f901.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2b102a3225400561cf38.png\" /></div>"},{"n":19,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A steel rod of 1 cm diameter and 5 cm length protrudes from a wall maintained at 100°C. The rod is insulated at its tip and is exposed to an environment with a convective heat transfer coefficient of 50 W/m<sup>2</sup>K and ambient temperature of 30°C. If the thermal conductivity of the rod is 30 W/ mK, then the efficiency of the fin is ______%. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[66,67],"answerText":"66.57","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>66.57 (66 - 67)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7d/7d57297a9a733fc13f1d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In a bank there is only one window. A solitary employee performs all the service required and the window remains continuously open from 7 am to 1 pm. It has been observed that an average of 54 clients arrive dring this period and the average service time per client is 5 minutes. The<br />\naverage waiting time of a client in the queue is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"10 min"},{"key":"B","html":"15 min"},{"key":"C","html":"20 min"},{"key":"D","html":"30 min"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8b/8b75049a4f966605d582.png\" /></div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>If <em>A</em> is a matrix such that <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/05/057516220292cbd39678.png\" /> then which of the following is/are true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>A</em> is non singular"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>A</em> is symmetric"},{"key":"C","html":"<em>A</em> cannot be skew-symmetric"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d8320a43819ed572cbc0.png\" />"}],"answer":["A","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fc4598fd3aab0de64726.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A fair coin is tossed 100 times. The probability of getting tails 1, 3, _ _ _ _ _ 49 times is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ffa78caa88dd9de3145d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/54b873d063c3aaeb2903.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4d/4d4558efa04096435d45.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b82cdb39d3cd4d03d3d3.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d9/d9cbeb0ec007b1270797.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/1786c855058d33646053.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":23,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>An air-water vapour mixture enters an adiabatic saturator at 30°C and leaves at 20°C, which is the adiabatic saturation temperature. The specific humidity in gram of water vapour per kg of dry air at the exit will be ________. [Correct upto one decimal place]<br />\nPressure corresponding to adiabatic saturation temperature to be taken as 2.339 kPa. Atmospheric pressure to be taken as 100 kPa.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[14.5,15.4],"answerText":"14.9","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>14.9 (14.5 - 15.4)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b08d03a41235eef14d31.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A differential band brake is shown in the figure below. The steel band has a thickness of 4 mm and a width of 110 mm. If the maximum permissible tensile stress in band is 50 MPa and maximum torque capacity of the brake is 5642 N-m, then the coefficient of friction between the friction lining and the brake drum is ______ [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/15/15230abfa8cde7fc279c.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.35,0.37],"answerText":"0.36","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.36 (0.35 - 0.37)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e1/e1d84dd0411762917fda.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d0/d0eb320ba5157ec6aa01.png\" /></div>"},{"n":25,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A prismatic bar of cross-sectional area 0.01 m<sup>2</sup> and length 2 m is subjected to axial forces as shown in the figure. The density and young’s modulus of the material are 8000 kg/m<sup>3</sup> and 260 GPa respectively.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fce8c62438adc7ef0f22.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The magnitude of normal stress at section <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d52059fa934d132aaab8.png\" /> is _____ kPa. [Rounded off to nearest integer]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1830,1880],"answerText":"1850","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1850 (1830 - 1880)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ed/ed2477899390b939d83a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4a/4a6e63067aa3c2f7e58e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":26,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Flat surface of a large cast-iron part measuring 2.5 m × 1.5 m × 0.4 m is to be machined using a planer along its face (2.5 m × 1.5 m). It is given that the approach and overtravel are 20 mm each, cutting speed is 25 m/min, return speed is 50 m/min, the machining allowance on either side of<br />\nthe plate width is 5 mm and feed is 1.5 mm/stroke. The machining time is ____ minutes. [Correct upto three decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[152.4,154.4],"answerText":"153.416","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>153.416 (152.400 - 154.400)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/89/892c43ae96df4e0e42ba.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c8/c8703dcc0be4df6c66e4.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A block of mass 2 kg rests on a smooth inclined plane making an angle of 30° with the horizontal.<br />\nIt is connected to another block of mass 3 kg by a cord passing over a frictionless pulley as shown in figure below. The acceleration of each block (in m/s<sup>2</sup>) is _____ . (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb4204167366913cb375.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3.8,4.1],"answerText":"3.924","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.924 (3.8 - 4.1)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/64/641fd20f6624991449de.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":28,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A pair of mating spur gears have 14.5° full depth teeth of module 10 mm. The pitch diameter of the smaller gear is 160 mm. If the transmission ratio is 3 : 2, then the addendum radius of the gear to avoid interference is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"116.5 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"124.5 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"126.5 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"123.2 mm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5f8673868aa29ca78899.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A 250 mm thick slab of a nickel alloy is subjected to cold rolled using a roll of diameter 450 mm. If the angle of bite during rolling is 10°, the maximum possible reduction (in mm) during rolling is ______ (Correct upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[6.6,7.4],"answerText":"6.854","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>6.854 (6.60 - 7.40)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5a/5a5f7d2c1e7a91cd06a8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":30,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The shape factor for an annular cylinder casting having an outside diameter of 50 cm, an inside diameter of 10 cm and a height of 40 cm, is _______. [Correct upto two decimal places]<br />\n(Take correction factor, <em>k</em> = 1.15)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5.6,6],"answerText":"5.84","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5.84 (5.60 - 6.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0b/0b2745c75f94e5f5365a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A hollow steel-shaft is to be replaced by an aluminium shaft of same external diameter. The material of the steel shaft is 27.5% stronger than aluminium shaft in shear. If steel is 2.75 times heavier than aluminium, then the percentage of weight saved by replacing steel with aluminium<br />\nfor same torque transmission is _______%. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[31,33],"answerText":"32.10","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>32.10 (31.00 - 33.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6d/6d941fa526ce49f53e5b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/20/20eaee796a8eb875c9d0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":32,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The angle between [1 1 0] and [1 1 1] directions in the cubic system is _______ degree. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[35,36],"answerText":"35.26","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>35.26 (35 - 36)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6a0c236e59281095f231.png\" /></div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A cylindrical pressure vessel with 2 m inside diameter is subjected to internal steam pressure of 2.5 MPa. The efficiency of riveted joint should be atleast 80%. The permissible stress for rivets in tension is 90 MPa and the corrosion allowance can be taken as 3 mm. Which of the following given below is/are correct for permissible thickness of plates and diameter of rivets?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Diameter of rivets is 39.8 mm."},{"key":"B","html":"Thickness of plate is 37.72 mm."},{"key":"C","html":"Thickness of plate is 42.74 mm."},{"key":"D","html":"Diameter of rivets is 36.85 mm."}],"answer":["B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/62/62879b9d090333f06dd1.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":34,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>With respect to exergy, the correct statements are</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"For an isolated system, the only processes allowed by the second law are those for which the exergy of the isolated system decreases."},{"key":"B","html":"The exergy balance of a system can be used to determine the locations, types and magnitudes of losses of the potential energy resources."},{"key":"C","html":"While energy is always conserved, exergy is not generally conserved."},{"key":"D","html":"When a closed system is allowed to undergo a spontaneous change from the given state to the dead state, its exergy is completely destroyed without producing any useful work."}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c, d)<br />\n&bull; Exergy of an isolated system can never increase, but always decreases.<br />\n&bull; Exergy balance find ways and means to reduce the losses so as to make the system more<br />\nenergy efficient and for more effective use of resources.</p>"},{"n":35,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<div> </div>\n\n<div><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/68/686fcac0d8a045c6275a.png\" /></div>\n\n<p>Then <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) is continuous at <em>x</em> = 4 when</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>a</em> = 0, <em>b</em> = 0"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>a</em> = 1, <em>b</em> = 1"},{"key":"C","html":"<em>a</em> = –1, <em>b</em> = 1"},{"key":"D","html":"<em>a</em> = 1, <em>b</em> = –1"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7b/7b2972b3ccd110b76951.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/82/82703e14baafb1f39748.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>For the given truss shown in the figure below. The number of zero force members are</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae2485040d19addd87dd.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"4"},{"key":"B","html":"5"},{"key":"C","html":"6"},{"key":"D","html":"7"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/561e6ce593a014ba70a2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":37,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Two steel sheets of equal thickness are joined by projection welding using a current of 30000A for 0.005s. The effective resistance of the joint is 100 μΩ. The welded joint can be assumed to be a cylindrical nugget of 5 mm diameter and 1.5 mm height. The density of steel is 7860 kg/m<sup>3</sup> and the heat required to melt steel is 10 J/mm<sup>3</sup>, the percentage of heat lost to the surrounding is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"34.40%"},{"key":"B","html":"34.55%"},{"key":"C","html":"65.45%"},{"key":"D","html":"65.60%"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8e0664c29ac1351636c2.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":38,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A heat pump is driven by a heat engine. The heat transfer from the heat engine and from the heat pump are used to heat the water circulating through the radiators of a building. The efficiency of the heat engine is 33% and the COP of the heat pump is 80% of carnot COP operating between 27°C and 127°C. The ratio of the heat transfer to the circulating water to the heat extracted by heat pump from cold space is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.634"},{"key":"B","html":"5.0.13"},{"key":"C","html":"3.268"},{"key":"D","html":"2.377"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ca/caee3e1063d3495b6b88.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A fluid particle at the point <em>r</em> = 2a, θ = <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/bc/bcea96b8585f0460c60e.png\" /> having a two-dimensional flow given by</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/de/debd64144f6e856c04b1.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The vorticity at the given point will be</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/40/401005720b3b7d879cfe.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1d/1dafceb184f72853deda.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/3416f25b01c7a87507b7.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"Zero"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6b8bce823e8ecc6e930e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A company produces an item at a rate of 4000 units per month. The set up cost per production is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/78f672fa073fb9109800.png\" /> holding cost/unit/month is <img algn=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/1d/1d97d71c443c75a81f71.png\" /> and the cost of one unit is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/dc/dc89b14676ae4fa802fc.png\" /> If the total annual cost is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ba/ba1ac19a0e9ab9d788a4.png\" /> then the monthly demand assuming optimal lot size is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1300 units"},{"key":"B","html":"792 units"},{"key":"C","html":"994 units"},{"key":"D","html":"333 units"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/7107bb678545cc698050.png\" /></div>"},{"n":41,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A cantilever beam of length L is loaded as shown in figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fa/fa13609ef7744e3044be.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The deflection at the free end is given by <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd87a9614b271864af36.png\" /> The value of α is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/539f87e632621bd990c2.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae8391e5298ed0709600.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1a/1aeb63c5054cbc493e25.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7b/7bb842da62020cc053ce.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/90/9039d623d5a4f6cd890b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0d/0d5069e494320cb78891.png\" /></div>"},{"n":42,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Degree of freedom for the linkage shown below is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/81/81a8b091a698afb6c8ba.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"4"},{"key":"B","html":"5"},{"key":"C","html":"6"},{"key":"D","html":"7"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e4/e4c811bc37175b578250.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In an orthogonal cutting the uncut chip thickness is 0.12 mm and the chip thickness after cutting is 0.225 mm. The cutting speed is 2 m/s and the width of cut is 6.25 mm. The measured cutting force is 60 kg and the thrust force is 25 kg. The rake angle of the tool is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d3/d3ea8ca4542705bd2581.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>The percentage of total energy that is being used to overcome friction at the tool chip interface is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"33.40%"},{"key":"B","html":"37.6%"},{"key":"C","html":"66.67%"},{"key":"D","html":"31.15%"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5c/5cdc76a21eda6fe9a51f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A 50 mm diameter steel rod supports a 9 kN load and in addition is subjected to a torsional moment of 100 Nm as shown below. What is the maximum tensile stress?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/024909d6928425c363c3.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"25.8 MPa"},{"key":"B","html":"25 MPa"},{"key":"C","html":"13.2 MPa"},{"key":"D","html":"Zero"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/98/984675eed00904533f79.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b093af548d2b63597db2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The pumping power required to maintain a steady flow in horizontal pipe of diameter 0.42 cm and length 11 m is 48.8 × 10<sup>–3</sup> W. The fluid flowing through the pipe has a specific gravity of 1.2 and dynamic viscosity of 1.44 × 10<sup>–3</sup> kg/m-s. Assuming fully developed laminar flow, the average velocity of flowing fluid is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.35 cm/s"},{"key":"B","html":"3.5 m/s"},{"key":"C","html":"35 cm/s"},{"key":"D","html":"5.3 m/s"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/90/900c5826c4c4b5a94148.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":46,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The following data is given for a four-stroke, single cylinder oil engine. During a trial of 30 minutes, the oil consumption is 4 litres, calorific value of the oil is 44 MJ/kg and its specific gravity is 0.732. The average area of indicator diagram is 7.5 cm<sup>2</sup>. The length of the indicator diagram is 7.5 cm and the spring constant is 550 kPa/cm. The engine speed is 210 rpm, the cylinder diameter is 30 cm and the stroke length is 40 cm. If the mechanical efficiency of the engine is 67% and the indicated thermal efficiency is 38%, then the brake specific fuel consumption will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.3214 g/kWh"},{"key":"B","html":"0.2153 g/kWh"},{"key":"C","html":"321.35 g/kWh"},{"key":"D","html":"215.3 g/kWh"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1ca1cb4e957b9bcd494d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The area enclosed between the curves <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d64f0ebd9563378fc4ee.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d82e27f5d8ab7aeb7864.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/12/129d112af101a52b7ff8.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/93/933dc824faa2864bd90a.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/02f8614369c0a2c4483c.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/60/60507f299e9dd26e1dce.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/af/af6ba28df931aac4acfc.png\" /></div>\n</div>"},{"n":48,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The solution of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/690011eef08ae35a67d2.png\" />  satisfying y(1) = 1 is given by</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a system of parabolas"},{"key":"B","html":"a system of circles"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/29/2954b253c9ab5c4a0a0e.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b6/b6ba0e97340f4ef3dbd6.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/28/28e97abd2c283955205f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f68b8271c94e93c72808.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A counter-flow double pipe heat exchanger is used to heat water from 20°C entering at a rate of 1.5 kg/s. The heating is to be done by geothermal brine water available at 165°C flowing at a mass flow rate of 2.25 kg/s. The specific heat capacities of water and geothermal brine water are 4.2 kJ/kgK and 4.32 kJ/kgK respectively. If the number of transfer units (NTU) is 0.65, then temperature of water leaving the heat exchanger after heating is ______ K. (Round off to nearest integer)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[353,355],"answerText":"354","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>354 (353 - 355)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/31/31f362b2df32040d69ea.png\" /></div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A piece of elastic material is subjected to three mutually perpendicular tensile stresses. The corresponding strains are in the ratio 7 : 8 : 9. If the greatest stress is 90 MPa, then the magnitude of maximum absolute shear stress is ______ MPa. [Correct upto two decimal places]<br />\nTake <em>K</em> = 150 GPa and G = 80 GPa.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3.7,3.97],"answerText":"3.83","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.83 (3.70 - 3.97)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/ac11f48efed158e58060.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Two sliders <em>s</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>s</em><sub>2</sub> slide on a rotating link as shown in the figure. The link rotates with an angular velocity of 2 rad/s and angular acceleration of 1 rad/s<sup>2</sup>.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8f/8f5caf2fd372d30d54ef.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The magnitude of absolute relative acceleration of slider <em>s</em><sub>2</sub> with respect to slider <em>s</em><sub>1</sub> is ____cm/s<sup>2</sup><br />\n(Correct upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1969,1971],"answerText":"1969.77","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1969.77 (1969 - 1971)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/be/be959dc77a1a5eee3ce0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A single-row roller bearing operates under a work cycle and designed for an expected life of 9800 hours with a reliability of 60%. During the cycle, it is subjected to a radial load of 6000 N at 400 rpm for 20% of time, a radial load of 9000 N at 600 rpm for 60% of time, and a radial load<br />\nof 8000 N at 500 rpm for remaining time.<br />\nThe dynamic load capacity of bearing is _______ kN. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[30,33],"answerText":"31.97","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>31.97 (30.00 - 33.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6ab53b37a859f7b6a1ad.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Eight jobs <em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em>, <em>D</em>, <em>E</em>, <em>F</em>, <em>G</em> and <em>H</em> are to be processed on a single machine. The processing time and due dates of the jobs are given below</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6d/6de9bd3a7bf0a08152a3.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The jobs are first sequenced according to the shortest processing time (SPT) rule. Then, they are sequenced based on the earliest due date (EDD) rule. The percentage change in average in process inventory when moving from the SPT sequence to the EDD sequence is ________ %. [Correct upto two decimal places]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[28,29],"answerText":"28.63","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>28.63 (28.00 - 29.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a4/a49fad36b124ccee322b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":54,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Air flows over a flat plate with uniform free stream velocity of U<sub>∞</sub>. At a certain location away from the leading edge the boundary layer thickness is 2.25 mm. The local wall shear stress is given by the expression τ = μu<sub>∞</sub>(a + 2<em>by</em>). The momentum thickness at that location is ______ cm.<br />\n[Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.03,0.03],"answerText":"0.03","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.03 (0.03 - 0.03)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/563bd092d1683b0b24fc.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2b569f3016bc8dc75b2d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A simply supported beam of length 4 m and carries a uniformly distributed load of 25 kN/m over its entire span. The cross-section of the beam is shown in the figure below. The maximum bending stress in the beam is _______ MPa. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c2/c2dbaae7916f11bb98b9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[108,113],"answerText":"110.57","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>110.57 (108 - 113)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b6/b6fca211fffabb591f94.png\" /></div>"},{"n":56,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>During electric-discharge drilling of a 10 mm × 10 mm square hole in a low carbon steel plate of 5 mm thickness, the resistance and capacitance in the relaxation circuits are 50 Ω and 10 μF respectively. The supply voltage is 200 V and the gap is maintained such that the sparking occurs at 150 V. The time required to complete the drilling operation is ____ hrs. [Rounded off to nearest integer]<br />\nUse, material removal rate (mm<sup>3</sup>/min) = (27.4) × (Power input in kW)<sup>1.54</sup></p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5,5],"answerText":"5","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7b/7b7113196496ba384fdb.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4ecd4ea67bd331c3c445.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Two discs are placed in two parallel planes, separated by a distance of 1 m and having same polar<br />\naxis. If disc-1 has diameter 200 mm, emissivity 0.8 and is at temperature 800 K. And disc-2 has<br />\ndiameter 2 m, emissivity 0.5 and is at temperature 300 K, then the net rate of radiation heat<br />\ntransfer between them is ________ W. [Correct upto two decimal places]<br />\nUse : <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/17fc54e6362879774394.png\" /> where <em>F</em><sub>12</sub> is shape factor of <em>A</em><sub>1</sub> with respect to <em>A</em><sub>2</sub>, <em>D</em> is diameter of disc-2 and <em>L</em> is separation between the discs.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[315,318],"answerText":"316.45","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>316.45 (315.00 - 318.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6b3ce1938cf851907c11.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/10/1067b874be9143fc2a00.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A ship is propelled by a turbine of mass 1000 kg running at 2000 rpm. The rotor has a radius of gyration of 1 m and rotates clockwise when viewed from stern. The ship pitches ±10° from the horizontal position with time period of 10 seconds in simple harmonic motion. The maximum magnitude of the gyroscopic couple developed on the ship is ______ kN-m (Correct upto two decimal).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[22,24],"answerText":"22.97","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>22.97 (22.00 - 24.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f0/f0f35ba13efd3ea10aa2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A refrigeration machine using R-12 as refrigerant operates between the pressures 2.5 bar and 9 bar. The compression is isentropic and there is no undercooling in the condenser. The vapour is in dry saturated condition at the beginning of the compression. The refrigerant<br />\nflow rate is 5 kg/min. If the actual COP is 0.65 of theoretical value, the net cooling produced per hour (in TR) is _____. (Correct upto two decimal values).<br />\nProperties of refrigerants are :</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/43/43114951469dd4f72c31.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Take <em>c<sub>p</sub></em> for superheated vapour at 9 bar as 0.64 kJ/kgK.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.7,1.8],"answerText":"1.76","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.76 (1.70 - 1.80)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/8387a4ea5e78c7618236.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":60,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Two involute gears in mesh have a module of 8 mm and pressure angle of 0.35 radian. The gear has 50 teeth and the pinion has 20 teeth. The addenda on 60<sup>th</sup> pinion and gear wheels are 1 module. The magnitude of ratio of sliding to rolling velocity at the beginning of contact is<br />\n________. (Correct upto three decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.35,0.38],"answerText":"0.362","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.362 (0.350 - 0.380)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d0/d0bda05d0ee362f93e78.png\" /></div>"},{"n":61,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>For a certain substance the specific heat at constant pressure varies with temperature as <em>C<sub>P</sub></em> = <em>a</em> + <em>bT</em>.<br />\nIf the temperature of the substance is increases at constant pressure from 127°C to 877°C, then which of the following statements given below is/are correct?<br />\nTake, (<em>C<sub>p</sub></em> )<em><sub>sub</sub></em> = 23.8 kJ/kg-K at 400 K and (<em>C<sub>p</sub></em>)<sub>sub</sub> = 29.05 kJ/kg-K at 1150 K.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The heat absorbed by the substance is nearly 19.818 kJ/kg."},{"key":"B","html":"The change in specific entropy of substance is nearly 27.427 kJ/kg-K."},{"key":"C","html":"The heat absorbed by the substance is nearly 19818.75 kJ/kg."},{"key":"D","html":"The change in specific entropy is nearly –27.427 kJ/kg-K."}],"answer":["B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4b/4bd74ffdd1bcaa588200.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The velocity field in a fluid is given as :</p>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/31/31503c79a6278f53ce4c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The flow is incompressible"},{"key":"B","html":"The flow is irrotational"},{"key":"C","html":"The acceleration experienced by the fluid particle is zero at (x = 0, y = 0, z = 0)"},{"key":"D","html":"The vorticity and circulation of the flow is zero"}],"answer":["B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b, c, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e9/e937a9769db572b205ea.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/04d8649796514f1c756c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":63,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In what direction from (3, 1, –2), the directional derivative of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/47/47ed4b296d6ce76fc546.png\" /> is maximum?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a1/a10a8fb7a7ab26e31a2d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cf/cfbb463a94fba7d3f31d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ff0bf22fe77bacb6c546.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6ae7b73cbf19f23c1f2e.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/66/6649e7056d86fbc6333c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The eigen values of the following matrix are represented by λ<sub>1</sub> and λ<sub>2</sub></p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/47/47b43ce22993f705ea35.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The value of<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/10/10ad8b2aa347291a1d6f.png\" />  is ________. [Correct upto two decimal places]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.3,0.35],"answerText":"0.33","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.33 (0.30 - 0.35)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/81/81db57fda5ada8874276.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":65,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Given a > 0, we wish to calculate its reciprocal value <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/1e/1e67eeeb8cba8e36ef35.png\" />  by using Newton Raphson method for <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) = 0. The Newton Raphson iteration formula for the function will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/67/6754d215b7d8b3e6902c.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cb5d004657ee1d020ff3.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a0/a02679af174a00b2e135.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c5/c5e834b39e0f0d3fcb16.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1d/1dc564b3cb5946a3a1f0.png\" /></div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":35,"MSQ":6,"NAT":24},"withoutKey":0}};
